  "summary_en": "Sweden's 2026 national AI Strategy, issued by the Government Offices, aims to put Sweden among the world's top ten AI nations. It is organised around three goals: societal benefit, sustainable development, and competitiveness and innovation. It calls for simple, technology-neutral regulation, wider data sharing, standards, AI in the public sector, computing capacity, skills and research. It replaces the 2018 national approach to AI.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Goal for Sweden to rank among the top ten AI nations globally",
   "Push for simplified, predictable, technology-neutral AI rules in Sweden and the EU, and for no new AI legislation until standards are in place",
   "Lay the foundations of an AI workshop for public administration in 2026, fully operational by 2030",
   "Expand computing capacity, data sharing, AI education and lifelong learning",
   "Agency for Digital Government and Swedish Post and Telecom Authority to support implementation, with an annual review"
